    "body": "@RReverser, as you say, #1280 was already a conformance error. In general, it's sad to have non-round-trippable conforming documents. We should treat such cases as spec bugs if feasible (i.e. make those cases non-conforming if feasible).\n\n@zcorpan, yes, it's likely that HTML consumers that use an XML pipeline internally would want to do infoset coercion regardless of the conformance status of the input.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
